# Discogs -> Kaggle monthly sync
#
# Runs every day at 06:00 server time. This is intentional, not a typo: the script checks
# state/published_months.json and exits in seconds if the current month is already
# published, so a daily run costs almost nothing on the days there's nothing to do. That
# removes the guesswork of picking a fixed "day of month" for when Discogs will have
# published - whenever it lands, this catches it within 24 hours instead of waiting for
# next month if a fixed day is missed.
#
# Install with: crontab -e   (then paste the line below, adjusting paths)

0 6 * * * cd /path/to/Discogs_Kaggle_Sync && /path/to/venv/bin/python run_monthly_sync.py --work-dir ./work --kaggle-owner ofurkancoban >> logs/sync.log 2>&1
